Trace first drawable lifecycle / on_first_present

This change applies to zed-industries/zed 90d8514059561f0e44af0a32e84e1c329cef3232
after patches/0001, 0002 and 0003.

What it does:
- Adds src/launch_trace.rs with on_first_present /
  on_first_drawable_completed. GPUI_LAUNCH_TRACE opt-in telemetry.
- Safety release is 250 ms after first commit, or three submitted
  drawables. This is a scheduling boundary, not verified scanout.

Metal presented-handler traces are not included: the renderer lives in
the git dep gpui_apple, which this crate does not fork. MacWindow::draw
counts a commit after renderer.draw returns, so the public API fires via
the safeties above (no silent no-op, no claim of scanout).

Three-way on 90d8514: gpui_macos.rs conflicted where #65058 removed
`pub(crate) use text_system::*` (CoreText text system moved to
gpui_apple::AppleTextSystem). Keep `pub use launch_trace::{...}`. Do
not restore the text_system re-export; the module is gone. platform.rs
and window.rs applied cleanly. The sharedApplication trace stays around
that call, then #64969's accessory policy.

Re-apply on a roll: git apply --3way patches/0004-first-drawable-lifecycle.patch
